{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he rebuked him, etc.</b> To remove the brothers' jealousy, he concealed the dream by means of the difficulty of ״I and your mother״ — for this constitutes an absolute refutation. The reason is that it would not enter the mind that the sons of Jacob could attain greatness over the nations except specifically from their father. And now there is no reality that his father would bow down to him; consequently he concealed the dream from the brothers, while his heart did not think so."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:22.793378625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}